PRIMARY COMPARATORS

SAME-FAMILY CROSS VIEW
Use A x B covariance.

If A and B share a measurement artifact,
the artifact appears in cross-view covariance.

CROSS-FAMILY VIEW
Use A x C covariance.

Family-specific errors are independent across A and C,
so only the true shared developmental signal should remain in expectation.

