PRIMARY POSITIVE
Cross-view covariance is NOT sufficient by itself.

The views must also be meaningfully independent with respect to their failure modes.

Same-family copies can turn shared noise into apparently persistent reusable structure.

Using cross-family evidence removes this failure completely in the tested family-specific-noise benchmark.

PRIMARY DESIGN RULE

TWO VIEWS
!=
TWO INDEPENDENT VIEWS.

Structural write should depend on:

EFFECTIVE INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE SOURCES

not:

raw number of measurements.

This is the same principle already observed in:
- context consensus;
- causal controls;
- relay provenance.

FALSE-GROWTH COST
